# THE ACME CLIENT THIS STACK BUILDS -- `PROD-01-TLS-ACME-01`, `R-146aa`, `AD-01`. Read as DATA by
# `infra/acme/Dockerfile` (at build time) and by `deploy.sh` (guard `acme-client-pinned`, before docker is
# touched): one NAME=VALUE per line, never sourced.
#
# WHAT IS PINNED. The base image is pinned by digest in the Dockerfile's `FROM` (the same Alpine digest
# `infra/minio/Dockerfile` pins). The client is the Alpine package `certbot`, pinned here by its EXACT
# package version, `<upstream version>-r<release>`, as `apk` prints it. A version that is not in this file
# cannot be installed: the Dockerfile refuses to build.
#
# WHY THE VALUE BELOW IS NOT A VERSION. The lane that wrote this had no network and no docker, and a
# version number written from memory is a claim about a package index nobody looked at. So the line says
# `UNRESOLVED`, and until a person with network access replaces it with what the index answers, `deploy.sh`
# refuses to deploy a host that has ALPHA_CERT_NAME set (`acme-client-pinned`) and so does the build. The
# one step, from any machine with docker (the runbook, section 6, step 1, prints the expected output):
#
#   docker run --rm alpine:3.22.1@sha256:4bcff63911fcb4448bd4fdacec207030997caf25e9bea4045fa6c8c44de311d1 \
#     sh -c 'apk update >/dev/null && apk policy certbot'
#
# then write the version of the repository this Alpine release serves (the line after the colon-less
# header, e.g. `4.1.1-r0`) below and commit it.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT PIN, said plainly: the packages `certbot` depends on float within Alpine 3.22's
# repository at build time. The image's identity is the base digest plus the client version, not a full
# lock of its dependency closure (the PostgreSQL and MinIO images are pinned harder than this).
ACME_CLIENT_APK_VERSION=UNRESOLVED
